{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "b6f1f0c2-8d4e-4a7b-9c1e-2f3a4b5c6d7e",
		"name": "Gradely API",
		"description": "Collection for the Gradely backend API, organized by module.\n\n## Setup\n1. Start the API with `pnpm run dev` (default `http://localhost:5000`).\n2. Seed the admin account with `pnpm run db:seed`. This reads `ADMIN_NAME`, `ADMIN_EMAIL`, and `ADMIN_PASSWORD` from `.env`.\n3. Import this collection into Postman.\n4. Run **Auth → Register Student** first. The test script stores `accessToken`, `refreshToken`, `studentId`, and `studentEmail` automatically.\n5. Run **Submissions → Create Submission**. The test script stores `submissionId` for the follow-up requests.\n6. For admin requests, run **Auth → Login Admin** using the seeded admin credentials.\n7. For reviewer workflows, run **Users → Create Reviewer (Admin)** to provision a reviewer, followed by **Auth → Login Reviewer** to save `reviewerAccessToken`.\n\n## Modules covered\n- **Health**: `GET /health`, `GET /`\n- **Auth**: `POST /api/v1/auth/register`, `POST /api/v1/auth/login` (Student, Reviewer, Admin), `PATCH /api/v1/auth/change-password`\n- **Users**:\n  - Profile: `GET /api/v1/users/me`, `PATCH /api/v1/users/me`\n  - Admin: `GET /api/v1/users` (list/filter/paginate), `POST /api/v1/users/reviewers` (create reviewer), `GET /api/v1/users/:id`, `PATCH /api/v1/users/:id` (update name/email/role/status), `PATCH /api/v1/users/:id/role` (role update), `DELETE /api/v1/users/:id` (cascade delete)\n- **Submissions**:\n  - Student: `POST /api/v1/submissions`, `GET /api/v1/submissions/me`, `PATCH /api/v1/submissions/:id`, `DELETE /api/v1/submissions/:id`\n  - Admin & Reviewer: `GET /api/v1/submissions`, `GET /api/v1/submissions/:id`, `POST /api/v1/submissions/auto-assign`, `PATCH /api/v1/submissions/:id/assign`, `PATCH /api/v1/submissions/:id/review`\n- **Feedbacks**:\n  - Admin: `GET /api/v1/feedbacks`, `GET /api/v1/feedbacks/:id`, `PATCH /api/v1/feedbacks/:id`\n- **Admin**:\n  - `GET /api/v1/admin/summary` (dashboard counters & monthly submission trends)\n\n## Variables\nAll variables are collection variables, so no environment file is required. Open the collection's **Variables** tab to edit `baseUrl`, `adminEmail`, or `adminPassword`.\n\n## Authentication cookies\nRegister and Login also set httpOnly `accessToken` / `refreshToken` cookies, and the API prefers the cookie over the `Authorization: Bearer` header. Postman keeps those cookies between requests, so after switching identities (for example, **Login Admin** after **Register Student**) the admin cookie overrides the student Bearer token. If a request unexpectedly returns `403`, clear the cookies for `localhost` (Postman → Cookies, or the cookie icon next to **Send**) and retry.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
